  "Valuation base FCF ($4.023B) is the 3-year average, but the filings analysis and key figures describe the FCF base as 'depressed' with FY26 FCF at $2.184B. A 'depressed base' cannot be $4.0B, which is 84% above the latest value. The notes say reliable=true with no caveats.",
  "Market Data forward P/E of 18.72x (implied EPS about $1.77) conflicts with the FY27 adjusted EPS guide of $1.15–$1.35 (implied P/E about 25–29x). The filings analysis uses the forward P/E to claim only a mild earnings dip.",
  "The base case assumes +3% FCF growth and a 3% terminal growth rate while the same analysis cites a guide for FY27 revenue down by a high-single-digit percent, Q1 revenue down 4.3%, and negative Q1 FCF. The growth rationale itself says nothing supports a recovery.",
  "The 'shares' field in Market Data (1.202B) is Class B only, whereas market cap implies about 1.484B and the 10-Q cover shows 1.485B. Any per-share figure using the 'shares' field would be about 23% too high. The filings analysis flags this, but the valuation notes list no issues, so it is unclear which count produced the per-share values.",
  "totalDebt of $11.125B in Market Data includes leases and does not reconcile to the filing ($7.893B plus $3.179B leases = $11.072B). Meanwhile the qualitative section calls the company 'net cash' with $8.4B cash. That holds only excluding leases (about $475M) and is not a strong position.",
  "Qualitative text says Q1 buybacks of $0 and dividends of $610M with 'sound' capital allocation, while also saying the dividend is not covered by FCF. The management rating of 'average' and the moat rating of 'narrow' do not square with a stock down about 78%, guidance resets and a brand-value cut of 25.9%.",
  "The catalyst of a 'margin recovery toward 12%' is listed in the same bullet as 'nothing provided confirms this recovery'. The scenario spread (bear -15%, base +42%, bull +105%) is skewed upward and has no scenario built on FY27 guidance, so the 'upside' is not probability-weighted.",
  "Qualitative text says the 10-Q shows 'SG&A fell 3%' and credits cost discipline, while demand creation rose 5.4% and operating overhead fell 6%. The cost cuts are partly severance-driven (about $300M in FY26), and adjusted EPS excludes about $0.15 of Pace costs, so it overstates run-rate profitability.",
  "The filings analysis notes that the 10-K text is XBRL metadata only, so all FY26 figures come from a single market-data feed, and the 10-Q is truncated (no MD&A, segment data or risk factors). The valuation is nonetheless labelled 'reliable', and key claims (China −26%, Jordan −mid-teens, Performance growth) come from secondary web sources rather than filings."
 ],
 "severity": "minor",
 "severity_reason": "The bullish conclusion is mostly an artifact of the model: a 3-year-average FCF base about 84% above the latest FCF, positive growth against guided revenue and EPS declines, and a forward P/E inconsistent with guidance. Corrected, intrinsic value falls to about $25–26 per share, and the 41% upside largely disappears. Those are valuation errors that remove the upside; they are not a reason to avoid the stock regardless of price. The company is still profitable, has a recognisable global brand and a manageable balance sheet (cash of $8.4B vs $7.9B financial debt). The uncovered dividend, working-capital drag and share loss are serious and would become major if FCF doesn't recover by FY27."
}
